 ### [Bhattacharyya Distance Coefficient](6998-bhattacharyya-distance-coefficient.md)
-The Bhattacharyya Distance Coefficient measures the overlap between two discrete probability distributions, specifically the histograms of voxel values inside and outside a target object in non-regular volumes. It serves as a density evaluation metric that quantifies how well the internal and external intensity distributions align, distinguishing itself from sibling methods like [Chamfer Distance](2446-chamfer-distance.md) by focusing on distributional similarity rather than geometric point-to-point proximity.
+The Bhattacharyya Distance Coefficient measures the overlap between two discrete probability distributions, specifically the histograms of voxel values inside and outside a target object in non-regular volumes. It serves as a density evaluation metric to quantify how well a reconstructed volume matches a target distribution. Unlike sibling methods such as Chamfer Distance which measure geometric point-to-point proximity, this method evaluates statistical distribution similarity.
+
+### [Plane Standard Deviation (Pσ) Calculation](7880-plane-standard-deviation-p-calculation.md)
+The Plane Standard Deviation (Pσ) metric evaluates the geometric accuracy of reconstructed planar surfaces in point clouds, specifically assessing how well a NeRF-generated point cloud aligns with ground-truth LiDAR data. It isolates planar structures by semantic grouping and measures the perpendicular spread of NeRF points relative to the estimated surface normal of the corresponding LiDAR plane. Unlike global metrics, Pσ focuses on local planar fidelity, making it distinct from general Chamfer Distance or neighbor-counting methods by explicitly accounting for surface orientation.
 
 ### Poisson Distribution Lookup for Feature Points
